{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"reveries@example.com","session":"agent:fix-ci-portability","created_at":"2026-10-04T02:50:39.763Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"actions/setup-node in the reveries-post-merge composite action failed on main with \"Relative pathing '.' and '..' is not allowed\": the cache-dependency-path was built as ${{ github.action_path }}/../../package-lock.json, and setup-node rejects unresolved '.' and '..' segments instead of normalizing them, so the action died before npm ci, the build, or synthesis ran. The same pattern was present in reveries-receive-check's setup-node step (a step that had not yet been reached) and in working-directory and node invocations in both actions.","decision":"Address the action source with plain repository-root paths. A composite run step with no working-directory already starts at the caller's checkout, so package-lock.json, npm ci, npm run build, and node scripts/<name>.mjs are all correct there; remove every github.action_path and '../' reference. Add packaging tests that reject github.action_path and any '../' or '/./' segment in a composite action and that tie each referenced file literal to an existing repository file.","impact":"The post-merge workflow can set up Node, install, build, and synthesize; the receive-check action cannot hit the same load-time failure when its setup-node step finally runs, which would otherwise break the required check. The guard makes the removal of a traversal a test failure instead of a live outage.","recurrence_control":"scripts/actions-packaging.test.mjs scans every composite action for github.action_path and relative segments and asserts each referenced file literal exists at the repository root. Verified by restoring main's manifests and observing four test failures naming all eight removed lines.","alternatives":["Drop the setup-node cache input from the actions","Fix only reveries-post-merge and leave reveries-receive-check latent","Use the absolute ${{ github.workspace }} for cache-dependency-path and working-directory"],"sources":[],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
